# Baked Apples

Based on [https://www.simplyrecipes.com/recipes/…](https://www.simplyrecipes.com/recipes/baked_apples) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251115052650/https://www.simplyrecipes.com/recipes/baked_apples))

{ rating="2" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 4 large [red baking apples]{ ing="red-baking-apples" } (2 apples)
- [ ] 1/4 cup [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" } (2 Tbsp)
- [ ] 1 tsp [cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" } (1/2 tsp)
- [ ] 1/4 cup [chopped pecans]{ ing="chopped-pecans" }, option (2 Tbsp)
- [ ] 1/4 cup [chopped raisins]{ ing="chopped-raisins" } (2 Tbsp)
- [ ] 1/4 Tbsp [butter per apple]{ ing="butter-per-apple" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup [boiling water]{ ing="boiling-water" } (3/4 cup)

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 375F
1. Core the [apples]{ ing="red-baking-apples" } leaving the bottom 1/2 inch intact
1. Place the [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }, [cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" }, [chopped raisins]{ ing="chopped-raisins" }, and [chopped pecans]{ ing="chopped-pecans" } (if using) in a small bowl and stir to combine. Place the [apples]{ ing="red-baking-apples" } in a baking dish and fill with the mixture
1. On each [apple]{ ing="red-baking-apples" }, place a 1/4 Tbsp of [butter]{ ing="butter-per-apple" } on top of the [sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }
1. Pour the [boiling water]{ ing="boiling-water" } into the bottom of the baking dish. Bake for 30-45 minutes, until tender but not overcooked and mushy. When done, baste with juices from the pan

## Notes

1. Try to look for Rome Beauty, Golden Delicious, or Jonagold
